      "line_number": 34,
      "line_end": 35,
      "title": "Search query built from request input",
      "description": "Search pastes the name query parameter straight into the SQL text with Sprintf. Quotes in name are not escaped. Any caller of GET /users can inject SQL and read or change any row in the database. Pass name to QueryContext as a bound parameter instead of formatting it into the query.",
      "suggested_change": "rows, err := h.DB.QueryContext(r.Context(), \"SELECT id, name FROM users WHERE name = ?\", name)",
      "source": "semgrep:go.lang.security.injection.tainted-sql-string.tainted-sql-string",
      "candidate": "c1",
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "Search pastes the name query parameter straight into the SQL text with Sprintf. Quotes in name are not escaped.",
      "consequence": "Any caller of GET /users can inject SQL and read or change any row in the database.",
      "fix": "Pass name to QueryContext as a bound parameter instead of formatting it into the query."
    },
    {
      "origin": "agent",
      "severity": "critical",
      "category": "bug",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "file_path": "internal/api/handler.go",
      "line_number": 63,
      "line_end": 63,
      "title": "Mutex left locked on missing key",
      "description": "Count locks h.mu and then returns early when key is empty without unlocking it. One request to GET /count without a key blocks every later Count request forever. Check key before taking the lock, or unlock with defer right after Lock.",
      "suggested_change": null,
      "source": "semgrep:trailofbits.go.missing-unlock-before-return.missing-unlock-before-return",
      "candidate": "c2",
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "Count locks h.mu and then returns early when key is empty without unlocking it.",
      "consequence": "One request to GET /count without a key blocks every later Count request forever.",
      "fix": "Check key before taking the lock, or unlock with defer right after Lock."
    },
    {
      "origin": "agent",
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "bug",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "file_path": "internal/api/handler.go",
      "line_number": 83,
      "line_end": 83,
      "title": "Response body closed before error check",
      "description": "fetchStatus defers resp.Body.Close before it checks err. When http.Get fails, resp is nil. An unreachable upstream makes the deferred Close panic with a nil pointer. The server then drops the GET /upstream request instead of answering 502. Move the deferred Close below the err check.",
      "suggested_change": null,
      "source": null,
      "candidate": null,
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "fetchStatus defers resp.Body.Close before it checks err. When http.Get fails, resp is nil.",
      "consequence": "An unreachable upstream makes the deferred Close panic with a nil pointer. The server then drops the GET /upstream request instead of answering 502.",
      "fix": "Move the deferred Close below the err check."
    },
